==Strategy==
Before Divine Cyclone even spawns, you're going to want to burst down the first Rain D. with [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] so that you don't have to deal with him during the main fight. Bring [[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Soractes]] and [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] to paralyze Divine Cyclone while doing chip damage, along with other [[:Category:Anti-Angel Cats|anti-Angel]] heavy hitters like [[Phantom Cat (Rare Cat)|Bubble Cat]], [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]] and [[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cat]] to cripple it. Deal as much damage as you can before Ange Lackey arrives to the frontlines; the quicker you can finish off Divine Cyclone, the better. Afterwards, cleanup is as simple as killing Ange Lackey and beating the stage.

